# Frontend SEO Internal Linking Policy (4626.fun)

This file owns canonical-only link safety and creator/vault/category link structure for frontend routes.

Scope:
- Apply only to user-facing frontend routes/components under `frontend/`.

Link safety:
- Link targets MUST be canonical URLs only (never parameterized sort/filter/pagination/tracking variants).
- Do not link to `noindex` routes when a canonical indexable hub/entity route exists.
- Prefer contextual in-content links over footer or sitewide link spam.

Creator route linking:
- MUST link to the creator's Vaults.
- MUST link to relevant Category/Tag hubs.
- SHOULD link to 3-5 contextually related Creators when appropriate.

Vault route linking:
- MUST link to its Creator route.
- MUST link to relevant Category/Tag hubs.
- SHOULD link to related Vaults when appropriate.

Category/Tag hub linking:
- SHOULD link to top Creators.
- SHOULD link to top Vaults.
- SHOULD link to related Category/Tag hubs.
